            <div xml:id="d753-a1">

                <pb facs="0586" n="504" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg504"/>

                <head>[Inclosures.]</head>
                <p>[The letter from the Attorney General and that from the United States attorney at
                    Waco are merely letters of transmission; the report transmitted is <pb
                        facs="0587" n="505" xml:id="pg505"/> from Deputy Marshal H. R. Hillebrand,
                    addressed to Marshal Nolte at San Antonio, and dated El Paso, May 12, 1911; it
                    narrates the writer’s personal investigation on the 8th and 9th of May, from
                    which he found that no shots had been fired from the American side of the river
                    and that there were ho facts on which to base or warrant the report contained in
                    the embassy’s memorandum.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
